{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"f2723ff4e167de39","name":"card_unit_the_deuce","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/CovertOp/units/card_unit_the_deuce","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"THE DEUCE","text":"Your Covert units cost 1 less to deploy.","flavorText":"The 502nd Parachute Infantry Regiment, nicknamed “The Deuce”, was an airborne unit of the US Army formed in 1942 which fought with the 101st Airborne Division during WWII. The 502nd were among the first paratroopers to drop behind enemy lines in Normandy on D-Day, where their job was to support the Allied amphibious attacks. The regiment continued fighting in Normandy until they returned to England for refitting at the end of June 1944. In September 1944 the regiment jumped again behind enemy lines, this time during Operation Market Garden. After successfully securing their objectives, the soldiers of the 502nd, alongside the rest of the 101st, advanced northward to occupy defensive positions on “The Island”, situated southwest of Arnhem. This location became the setting for some of the 101st's toughest battles during their operations in the Netherlands. In December 1944, during the Battle of the Bulge, the 502nd along with the 101st Airborne Division, played a crucial role in defending the town of Bastogne. As the war was nearing its end the regiment was moved to the Ruhr Pocket to help in mop-up operations, and on 5th of May they managed to secure Hitler's private residence in the town of Berchtesgaden. During the summer of 1945 the regiment was sent in Austria on occupation duty, before being shipped back to the US and deactivated in November.","faction":"USA","type":"infantry","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":1,"operationCost":2,"attack":2,"defense":2},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_the_deuce","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_the_deuce_title","SourceString":"THE DEUCE","LocalizedString":"THE DEUCE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":2,"defense":2,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_the_deuce_text","SourceString":"Your Covert units cost 1 less to deploy.","LocalizedString":"Your Covert units cost 1 less to deploy."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_the_deuce_history","SourceString":"The 502nd Parachute Infantry Regiment, nicknamed “The Deuce”, was an airborne unit of the US Army formed in 1942 which fought with the 101st Airborne Division during WWII. The 502nd were among the first paratroopers to drop behind enemy lines in Normandy on D-Day, where their job was to support the Allied amphibious attacks. The regiment continued fighting in Normandy until they returned to England for refitting at the end of June 1944. In September 1944 the regiment jumped again behind enemy lines, this time during Operation Market Garden. After successfully securing their objectives, the soldiers of the 502nd, alongside the rest of the 101st, advanced northward to occupy defensive positions on “The Island”, situated southwest of Arnhem. This location became the setting for some of the 101st's toughest battles during their operations in the Netherlands. In December 1944, during the Battle of the Bulge, the 502nd along with the 101st Airborne Division, played a crucial role in defending the town of Bastogne. As the war was nearing its end the regiment was moved to the Ruhr Pocket to help in mop-up operations, and on 5th of May they managed to secure Hitler's private residence in the town of Berchtesgaden. During the summer of 1945 the regiment was sent in Austria on occupation duty, before being shipped back to the US and deactivated in November.","LocalizedString":"The 502nd Parachute Infantry Regiment, nicknamed “The Deuce”, was an airborne unit of the US Army formed in 1942 which fought with the 101st Airborne Division during WWII. The 502nd were among the first paratroopers to drop behind enemy lines in Normandy on D-Day, where their job was to support the Allied amphibious attacks. The regiment continued fighting in Normandy until they returned to England for refitting at the end of June 1944. In September 1944 the regiment jumped again behind enemy lines, this time during Operation Market Garden. After successfully securing their objectives, the soldiers of the 502nd, alongside the rest of the 101st, advanced northward to occupy defensive positions on “The Island”, situated southwest of Arnhem. This location became the setting for some of the 101st's toughest battles during their operations in the Netherlands. In December 1944, during the Battle of the Bulge, the 502nd along with the 101st Airborne Division, played a crucial role in defending the town of Bastogne. As the war was nearing its end the regiment was moved to the Ruhr Pocket to help in mop-up operations, and on 5th of May they managed to secure Hitler's private residence in the town of Berchtesgaden. During the summer of 1945 the regiment was sent in Austria on occupation duty, before being shipped back to the US and deactivated in November."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::CurrentExpansion","isReserved":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardReset","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardSpawnedInHand","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDrawnFromDeck"],"draftBaseWeight":0.9,"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/CandidateArtwork/Summer_24/t_the_deuce.t_the_deuce","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Ken Smith","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/THE_DEUCE.THE_DEUCE","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":363.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_the_deuce_photo","SourceString":"Soldiers of the 101st Airborne Division in Carentan, France, 1944.","LocalizedString":"Soldiers of the 101st Airborne Division in Carentan, France, 1944."},"blowU